invariant: INV-14
file: suite.h
catches: webpki_session_aes_runtime
reason: an AES=runtime init admits ch_cfg.aes_instructions at 0, the value a
  caller that never set the field leaves, and the session runs as though
  the caller had answered that the instructions are absent. The ruling is
  that every caller states what its probe found (docs/decisions.md 81).
  The edit keeps 3 refused, so it moves the lower edge alone;
  test_webpki_runtime_answers requires ch_connect to refuse 0 before a
  byte leaves.

--- old
    return cfg->aes_instructions == CH_AES_INSTRUCTIONS_PRESENT ||
           cfg->aes_instructions == CH_AES_INSTRUCTIONS_ABSENT;
--- new
    return cfg->aes_instructions <= CH_AES_INSTRUCTIONS_ABSENT;
